<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Kalgold Q1 pre-capex net loss deepens.</title>
<headline>Kalgold Q1 pre-capex net loss deepens.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Quarter to end-March versus preceding quarter</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Net loss before capital spending</p>
<p>					  1.67  vs 0.27</p>
<p>    Capital spending		1.86  vs 4.17</p>
<p>    Ore crushed		  282,000  vs 208,000</p>
<p>    Gold output (kg)	     184.4  vs 137.2</p>
<p>    Yield (gram/t)		  0.65  vs 0.66</p>
<p>    Cost (rand/kg)		 55.67  vs 90.79</p>
<p>    Revenue (rand/kg)	    50.31  vs 55.94</p>
<p>Full name: Kalahari Goldridge Mining Co Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - Directors said the capital expenditure on mining assets relates mainly to costs incurred on extensions to the carbon-in-solution circuit in the gold recovery plant.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
